  <section class="agtm-definition-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label">The simple answer</div>
      <h2>What is AI GTM?</h2>
      <p><strong>AI GTM means using artificial intelligence to improve how a company goes to market.</strong></p>
      <p>In simple English, AI helps a sales team sort through more companies, data, changes, contacts, and activity than people can review manually. It can help identify which accounts fit, where something important may be happening, who matters inside the company, and what information a salesperson should understand before reaching out.</p>
      <p>AI does not create demand by itself. It does not prove that a buyer has budget, authority, urgency, or a reason to change. CallTeam connects the intelligence to human outreach so the market can confirm what is real.</p>
      <div class="agtm-truth-line">The purpose of AI GTM is not more automated activity. It is better commercial attention.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="agtm-problem-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">The data is not the motion</div>
      <h2>Most companies have signals. Few know what to do next.</h2>
      <p class="agtm-section-intro">A business can own an enormous database and still have no clear answer to five basic questions: which account matters, why now, who should care, what should be said, and who owns the next action.</p>
      <div class="agtm-problem-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Too much data</h3><p>Lists, CRM records, website activity, event leads, intent feeds, and market information accumulate faster than the team can evaluate them.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Weak priorities</h3><p>Every account looks equally important, so sellers work whatever appears first instead of the strongest combination of fit and timing.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Signals without context</h3><p>An alert appears, but nobody checks whether the event connects to the offer, buyer, problem, or commercial situation.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Research without action</h3><p>Account information sits in a dashboard while no person owns the call, follow up, qualification, or next decision.</p></article>
        <article><span>05</span><h3>Automation without judgment</h3><p>Generic messages are triggered from weak assumptions and sent at scale before anyone verifies relevance.</p></article>
        <article><span>06</span><h3>No learning loop</h3><p>Objections, referrals, timing, bad data, and buyer language disappear instead of improving the next account decision.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

