  <section class="agtm-signals-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">Buying signals and business triggers</div>
      <h2>Look for a stronger reason to investigate the account now.</h2>
      <p class="agtm-section-intro">Signal availability depends on the market, data sources, permissions, and engagement. The purpose is to improve where the team investigates, not pretend an event guarantees a purchase.</p>
      <div class="agtm-signal-map">
        <article><span>COMPANY CHANGE</span><h3>Something inside the business moved</h3><ul><li>Funding or expansion</li><li>Leadership appointments</li><li>New locations or markets</li><li>Product launches</li><li>Hiring or role creation</li><li>Restructuring or pressure</li></ul></article>
        <article><span>BUYER ACTIVITY</span><h3>Someone engaged or returned</h3><ul><li>Website activity when available</li><li>Content or event engagement</li><li>Form submissions</li><li>Email responses</li><li>Previous conversations</li><li>Referral activity</li></ul></article>
        <article><span>SALES HISTORY</span><h3>The company already knows something</h3><ul><li>Stalled opportunities</li><li>Closed lost accounts</li><li>Former customers</li><li>Untouched inbound leads</li><li>Old target accounts</li><li>Contacts changing companies</li></ul></article>
        <article><span>MARKET CONTEXT</span><h3>The operating environment changed</h3><ul><li>Technology adoption</li><li>Vendor or platform changes</li><li>Regulatory developments</li><li>Category movement</li><li>Competitive pressure</li><li>Operational priorities</li></ul></article>
      </div>
      <div class="agtm-signal-warning"><strong>A signal is a reason to investigate.</strong><span>A human conversation determines whether there is fit, need, interest, timing, authority, and a useful next step.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="agtm-priority-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">Account prioritization</div>
      <h2>Fit tells us who could buy. Timing tells us where to look first.</h2>
      <div class="agtm-priority-board" role="img" aria-label="Account priority matrix comparing ideal customer fit and signal strength">
        <div class="agtm-axis-y"><span>HIGH FIT</span><span>LOW FIT</span></div>
        <div class="agtm-matrix">
          <article class="watch"><small>STRONG FIT · WEAK SIGNAL</small><strong>WATCH AND DEVELOP</strong><p>Right company, limited evidence of movement. Research, monitor, or work through a deliberate outbound motion.</p></article>
          <article class="attack"><small>STRONG FIT · STRONG SIGNAL</small><strong>INVESTIGATE NOW</strong><p>Account quality and current evidence justify deeper research, buyer mapping, and timely human outreach.</p></article>
          <article class="deprioritize"><small>WEAK FIT · WEAK SIGNAL</small><strong>DEPRIORITIZE</strong><p>Little commercial reason to spend valuable research and calling capacity here.</p></article>
          <article class="verify"><small>WEAK FIT · STRONG SIGNAL</small><strong>VERIFY BEFORE ACTION</strong><p>Activity may look exciting, but the account still needs to match the offer and buying logic.</p></article>
        </div>
        <div class="agtm-axis-x"><span>WEAK SIGNAL</span><span>SIGNAL STRENGTH →</span><span>STRONG SIGNAL</span></div>
