  <section id="faq" class="agtm-faq-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">AI GTM FAQ</div>
      <h2>Questions B2B teams ask before building an AI assisted go to market motion.</h2>
      <div class="agtm-faq-list">
        <details><summary>What does AI GTM mean?</summary><p>AI GTM means using artificial intelligence to improve how a company goes to market. It can support market selection, ideal customer definition, account discovery, buying signal investigation, buyer research, account prioritization, outreach preparation, workflow, measurement, and continuous learning.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What are AI GTM services?</summary><p>AI GTM services help a company design and operate an AI assisted go to market motion. CallTeam connects the market, data, signals, research, account priorities, human outreach, qualification, reporting, and feedback needed to turn intelligence into commercial action.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What is signal led GTM?</summary><p>Signal led GTM uses relevant business events, buyer activity, sales history, or market changes to help prioritize where a sales team investigates and acts. The signal improves timing and context, but it still requires fit, verification, outreach, and qualification.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What are B2B buying signals?</summary><p>B2B buying signals are observable events or actions that may indicate change, interest, need, or timing inside an account. Examples can include hiring, expansion, leadership changes, technology changes, website activity when available, event engagement, previous conversations, and reopened sales activity.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can AI identify companies that are ready to buy?</summary><p>AI can identify accounts showing stronger fit, change, activity, or possible need. A signal is not proof that a company will buy. CallTeam uses research and human conversations to test whether the signal represents a real business situation and a useful next step.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What is the difference between account fit and buying intent?</summary><p>Account fit describes whether a company matches the profile that can realistically use and buy the offer. Intent describes evidence that a company or person may be researching, changing, engaging, or moving. Strong priority usually requires useful fit and credible timing evidence.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Which signals can CallTeam investigate?</summary><p>The available signal set depends on the client, market, data, permissions, and sources. It can include company changes, hiring, leadership activity, technology movement, website or content activity when available, CRM history, previous opportunities, events, responses, referrals, and other agreed business triggers.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does CallTeam build prospect lists?</summary><p>CallTeam can build or refine an ICP matched account and contact universe, or work with a client CRM, named account list, event list, inbound source, previous opportunity set, or other approved data.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can CallTeam research named accounts?</summary><p>Yes. Account research can organize company context, relevant people, possible business problems, current changes, signal evidence, contact information, and useful preparation for a human sales conversation.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can CallTeam work with our CRM?</summary><p>CallTeam can work with an agreed CRM or operating workflow when access, fields, permissions, routing rules, data responsibilities, and security expectations are clear. Another structured process can be used when direct access is not appropriate.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can AI GTM reactivate old leads?</summary><p>Yes. Old inbound leads, previous conversations, stalled opportunities, closed lost accounts, former customers, and dormant target accounts can be reviewed for new contacts, company changes, improved fit, or a stronger reason to reconnect.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is AI GTM the same as an AI SDR?</summary><p>No. An AI SDR usually refers to software or an agent performing parts of prospecting, messaging, qualification, or scheduling. AI GTM is the broader system connecting market logic, data, signals, research, people, workflows, execution, and learning.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does CallTeam use AI to make sales calls?</summary><p>CallTeam uses AI where it improves research, organization, prioritization, context, analysis, and workflow. Human salespeople handle live calling, listening, objections, qualification, and next step decisions.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How is AI GTM different from AI lead generation?</summary><p>AI lead generation focuses on finding, researching, enriching, and prioritizing potential accounts and contacts. AI GTM is the broader operating system connecting market strategy, data, signals, account intelligence, outreach, qualification, workflow, measurement, and feedback.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How is AI GTM different from outsourced SDR services?</summary><p>AI GTM defines and connects the intelligence, priorities, signals, research, workflow, and learning around the market. Outsourced SDR services provide the managed people and daily execution required to research, call, follow up, qualify, and book meetings.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How is AI GTM different from the 90-Day Revenue Engine?</summary><p>AI GTM focuses on the intelligence to action system around market selection, account priorities, signals, research, activation, and feedback. The 90-Day Revenue Engine addresses the wider revenue operation, including ICP, CRM, pipeline process, roles, reporting, management rhythm, and sales execution.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How should AI GTM performance be measured?</summary><p>Measurement can include account and contact quality, signal relevance, research completion, response time, conversations, buyer outcomes, qualification, meetings, accepted handoffs, opportunities, segment performance, and the quality of market learning.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How much do AI GTM services cost?</summary><p>Pricing depends on market scope, data condition, signal sources, research depth, account volume, workflow requirements, outreach execution, CRM involvement, reporting, and the amount of ongoing management required.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What does implementation require from our team?</summary><p>The client provides offer knowledge, proof, approved claims, access decisions, commercial boundaries, sales availability, and timely feedback. CallTeam defines the exact operating responsibilities before implementation begins.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How do we start?</summary><p>Start with a strategy call. CallTeam reviews the offer, market, ICP, current data, signal sources, tools, sales capacity, CRM workflow, qualification standard, and the commercial decision the AI GTM motion needs to support.</p></details>
